                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Big Reveal", body: "Here's something that will either excite you or annoy you:\n\nEvery single concept in this course — shadow, ego death, unity consciousness, kundalini, dark night, planes of existence — has a measurable correlate in modern neuroscience.\n\nThe mystics described the experience. The scientists measured the mechanism. They're looking at the same elephant from different angles.\n\nRumi said: \"You are not a drop in the ocean. You are the entire ocean in a drop.\"\n\nA neuroscientist would say: \"During advanced meditation, the default mode network — the brain's self-referencing circuit — downregulates, and the boundary between self-representation and world-representation dissolves, producing a subjective experience of unity.\"\n\nSame thing. One is poetry. One is an fMRI readout. Both are accurate.\n\nThis module maps every key awakening concept to peer-reviewed brain science. Not to \"prove\" mysticism right — but to show that these aren't competing worldviews. They're complementary measurement systems describing the same reality.\n\nIf you're a skeptic: good. Skepticism is healthy. But dismiss the data at your own loss.\nIf you're spiritual: good. This will deepen your understanding of what's actually happening in your nervous system during the experiences you've had.\n\nEither way — citations included. Check them yourself."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Three Brain Networks You Need to Know", body: "Before we map anything, you need to understand three brain networks. These are the key players in every awakening phenomenon.\n\nTHE DEFAULT MODE NETWORK (DMN)\nThe \"Me\" circuit. Active when you're thinking about yourself — replaying the past, planning the future, maintaining your sense of identity. It's the neural basis of ego.\n\nWhen the DMN is hyperactive: rumination, anxiety, depression, rigid self-concept. The Sleepwalker stage — endlessly thinking about \"me, me, me\" without awareness.\n\nWhen the DMN quiets: ego dissolution, present-moment awareness, flow states, mystical experiences. The Unity Consciousness stage.\n\nStudy: Brewer et al. (2011) — Experienced meditators show significantly reduced DMN activity during meditation, correlating with reduced self-referential thinking.\n\nTHE SALIENCE NETWORK (SN)\nThe \"What Matters\" circuit. Decides what deserves attention. Tags prediction errors — things that don't match your model of reality.\n\nOveractive SN + Shadow material = anxiety, hypervigilance, projection (everything feels like a threat because your model is full of unprocessed fear).\n\nBalanced SN = accurate threat detection, appropriate emotional response, synchronicity recognition (noticing meaningful patterns without paranoia).\n\nTHE CENTRAL EXECUTIVE NETWORK (CEN)\nThe \"Focus\" circuit. Directed attention, problem-solving, integration of information across brain regions.\n\nStrong CEN = good emotional regulation, clear decision-making, integration of unconscious material.\n\nThe goal of every contemplative practice across history — meditation, prayer, contemplation, shadow work — is the same neurologically: quiet the DMN, balance the SN, strengthen the CEN. Different traditions. Same neural target."),
